Z||000000||BigTurbo87GT||03-07-2001||11:06 AM||||Hey guys! I'm getting sucked into a complete rebuild of my GT. The end result will have to stand up to 14 psi or more of boost so I wanna stud everything that I can with ARP bolts. Problem is, I can't find part numbers for even the major fasteners (Heads and Mains/Rods). Does anyone have a source for a kit or some individual part numbers?<P>Thanks a whole lot for any help, Bill<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||03-07-2001||11:51 AM||||I know the Fiero store stocks ARP's for the V6. Maybe someone on the forum has gotten them and knows the Part#.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hartz||03-07-2001||01:30 PM||||I've got the ARP Head and Main studs, washers, nuts, rod bolts, etc., but don't have the P/N's in front of me.  If you don't have them by end of day, shoot me an e-mail, and I'll look them up when I get home.<P>My pistons I had to have made custom.  I went with JE forged pistons.  They give a nice 8.57 CR for my turbo.<P>Best of luck,<BR>Hartz<BR>'85 SE V6 Turbo||||reg||11
Z||000003||BigTurbo87GT||03-07-2001||01:58 PM||||Thanks Guys.<BR>Hey Hartz, you sound like a guy I really need to talk to! Could/would you share some engine specs?  8.5 is where I think I wanna be and it sounds like maybe you've been where I'm planning on going. Did you do a custom turbo or a kit?||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrossum||03-07-2001||03:12 PM||||i have everything in my stroked 4 cyl studded with arp studs. i called arp directly and talked with a young lady named Cammy. she got me eveything i needed and even put up with my ignorance at times. number is 800-826-3045. hope this helps....||||reg||10
Z||000005||Hartz||03-08-2001||12:38 AM||||OK, I came home and dug out the paper work on the engine.  I can't tell for sure, but I think the P/N is 133-6002 for the set.  Probably best to double check when you order.  <P>Yeah, I'd be happy to talk about my engine.  The turbo was a kit from a company in Canada, but when I went to install the kit, it turned out it wasn't very good, and I ended up junking half of it and fabricating a lot of stuff.  The engine was completely redone, balanced, blueprinted, new cam, port matched intake and exhaust, some decent head work, etc.  It ended up costing a small fortune, but I am pretty happy with the results.  <P>I've got all the details on the pistons if you need them.  If you've got questions, e-mail me.  I'm going to be off the board for the next few days, but I'll be back next week.<P>Take care,<BR>Hartz<P>85 SE V6 Turbo||||reg||1
Z||000006||G-Nasty||03-08-2001||12:49 AM||||14 lbs boost may be too much- 8 is common.  Keep a log on everything you do because I am also wanting to do the same thing...If it worx. Gotta keep up with the jones' AKA Supras &  Stangs somehow. Off the line its no prob but mid is not there. I think a spooled up V6 can do the trick.<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||BigTurbo87GT||03-08-2001||11:18 AM||||For a stock engine 14 probably would be, but I definitely won't be stock. Maybe even a stock engine could stand up to 14 psi if properly intercooled and good ignition control is implemented (knock sensor driving retard, like a J&S system).<BR> I have some ideas for fabricating fiberglass ductwork to facilitate an air-to-air intercooler in rear lower quarters.<BR>There is an excellent book by Corky Belle (sp?) called Maximum Boost that is a great reference and starting point for turbo charging anything. You can find it at Amazon.com, I think it was $15 or so.<BR>||||reg||1
